# Security headers for the STATIC assets.
#
# Trap this exists for: on Workers, static assets are served by the assets
# binding and NEVER reach the Worker, so they only obey this file. Routes that
# the Worker renders (/, /api/*) take their headers from next.config.ts instead.
# With only one of the two, half the site ships without HSTS.
#
# No Content-Security-Policy on purpose: AstralFlow renders React inline styles
# (the chart wheel, the ACG map, the resonance rings) and a strict style-src
# would silently kill them in production only.
#
# No `Cache-Control: immutable` here either, deliberately. Asking for a missing
# asset can fall through to the Worker and get an HTML response, and an
# immutable HTML answer freezes at the edge for a year with no way to purge it.
# Next already fingerprints and caches /_next/static/* correctly on its own.

/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=()
